Z||000000||Sage||11-19-2001||11:23 AM||||I have an HP Pavilion model# X50 monitor.  The cpu is an HP Pavilion #4530.  The display is so dark that I can't see the details in most picture posts.  There are no physical adjustments on the monitor itself.  I am using the correct driver for the monitor and have the on screen setting as light as it will go.  <P>Anybody have any suggestions or information to get it to display properly, or at least lighten it up so I can see the picture posts better?<P>Thanks for any help or ideas.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||5
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||11-19-2001||12:16 PM||||get it checked out quickly since its prob still under warranty..  looks like the tube is going (mine went 3 months ago)   they normally have a 3 yr warranty on monitors..<P><BR>Turn it off when your not using it, a friends monitor caught fire before when the tube shorted out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||11-19-2001||04:01 PM||||Thanks for the input.  If it gets any worse, I will take it in to be looked at.<P> It has been this way since new.<P>  Probably wouldn't have noticed anything was wrong, but my son brought up a pic on it that he had looked at on his and noticed that it didn't show up the same way on mine as on his. <P> Up to this point I just attributed not being able to discern details to bad pics, but after noting the difference between mine and his, it became apparent that this monitor displays everything dark.<P>It hasn't really changed at all since I started using it, so if it is the tube, it was bad from the start, but it hasn't gotten any worse or different than it ever was.<P>Thanks again.<P>Any other ideas?  Maybe a different driver?<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||11-19-2001||04:08 PM||||hmmmmmmm.  I have worked on computers for a living now for 10 years, and have never seen a monitor with no external controls.  No wheels?  No menu buttons?  Not under the lip in the front?  Not on the side?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Reality||11-19-2001||04:26 PM||||GET A NEW MONITOR THAT ONE SUX!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>No he dosen't have external controls. What is on the monitor is a button for a menu control. But in the menu section the only options you get is two different ones. One turns the colour to blue one to red. It is quite irritateing. There are options for brightness and contrast but they are already turned all the way up. Seriously you can't see anything on that thing. Okay that's my rant  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Have a good one. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Sage||11-19-2001||04:31 PM||||I thought the same thing.<P>  This is not the first monitor I've had.  All the others had some type of external manual controls for contrast and bright, if nothing else.<P>  I've looked this thing over top to bottom, front to back and side to side and don't see a thing!  This is a unit that was purchased by my wife who knows less about computers than I do.  Works fine other than that minor detail!  I will look it over some more.<P>  Had one, a Packard Bell, I think, that had a little hidden door that you had to push on to open, and that's where the external controls were!<P>Thanks for the input, I will keep looking.<P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
